  "slug": "cryo-structure-34d6",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and one published study report automated, statistically defined alternatives to sequential cryo-EM and cryo-ET processing steps.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is replacing sequential or manually tuned steps in cryo-EM and cryo-ET density processing with integrated, differentiable, or statistically defined procedures. End2EndPtychoSPA fits a 3D potential and particle poses jointly to 4D-STEM data through a differentiable multislice model, rather than reconstructing sequentially. Astex-Faro applies a reference-ensemble statistical framework, with a new FSCoh consistency metric, to flag significant density deviations in cryo-EM maps for drug discovery hit identification. RobPicker, a meta-learning framework, corrects label noise and reweights rare species to improve macromolecule particle picking in cryo-ET tomograms. Ramped phase randomization offers a low-pass filter variant for cryo-EM map comparison and neural network data augmentation, with an open-source Python implementation. The thread is methodological rather than experimental, and the items address distinct tasks; the shared element is computational statistical or learned treatment of noisy density data.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-06"
}
